==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# The liquid [[extract]] of [[lemon]] fruit, notably [[sour]] and often [[condensed]], as used especially in food preparation.
# The juice of a [[sweet lemon]] or [[sweet lime]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Danny Lane|title=Black Silk Pajamas|publisher=Xlibris Corporation|isbn=9781462828906|page=158
|passage=“Come and eat,” said my father. Everyone else had already eaten lunch, so my mother waited on me. First she gave me a tall glass of '''lemon juice''', followed by white noodles, egg rolls, cucumber salad, fish sauce, and meat rolled in rice bread.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Vithal Rajan|title="Not So!" Stories for Older Children|isbn=9788181575586|page=63
|passage=They wiped his face with a hot towel, gave him a tall glass of very refreshing '''lemon juice''', and took his temperature, after making him comfortable on a nice clean soft bed inside the ambulance, which sped along its siren wailing.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Madeline Scherb|title=A Taste of Heaven: A Guide to Food and Drink Made by Monks and Nuns|publisher=Penguin|isbn=9781101133392
|passage=Spiritual pilgrims can console themselves for giving in to their appetites by making sure to buy fromage made by the monks of Cîteaux; pick up some good bread and sparkling '''lemon juice''' to go with the cheese and have a picnic on the way to the abbey.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Deepak Dalal|title=Sahyadri Adventure: Koleshwar's Secret|publisher=Westland|isbn=9789383260676
|passage=Smita Dongre settled Vikram on the sofa and a young lady dressed in a bright salwar kameez placed '''lemon juice''' and biscuits on the table. [...] Vikram sipped sugary '''lemon juice'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2014|author=Ale-esi Makgekgenene|chapter=Sanitas Tea Garden a place to unwind|chapterurl=http://www.sundaystandard.info/print_article.php?NewsID=21065|title=Sunday Standard
|passage=Upon seating, guests are treated to a complimentary free glass of thirst quenching '''lemon juice''' with ice.}}

